validate]} {:db/id "q-332833/field-9" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a1aa9c-6b39-585a-9542-83855f47107a" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-332833/field-9/358ccb7152cbb4f2d401a026779746d5a4778f72e6ce20992ca89f5a558abcd2" :answer-field/choices ["q-332833/field-9/4d10c8aad14d212d9d75d8ad1d951f701246a81dfad097c3ef54f88979b8b298" "q-332833/field-9/358ccb7152cbb4f2d401a026779746d5a4778f72e6ce20992ca89f5a558abcd2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332833" :question/id #uuid "fe606e21-16dc-5275-bda3-617803b9b0bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-332833" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }-1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}\\cdot {{field-1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}\\cdot {{field-2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{-t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}}\nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-5}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/f1335e5420fe6e475cded1092e9b1ba621e0d88f46110b69ffef5e35ed080d6e.png)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-6}}\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line.\n\nSince ${e}^{2t}\\to $ \n{{field-7}}\nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-8}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/a53bb4e6cd7552b92424b168d0cda90fa1085b5e72fbf8a3c37a3a948bdcf9ad.png)\n\nThe {{field-9}}  of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/ecccffb89d43b8de4ce0952d9b8d9686e74670b4d86b29687c76355b70a6ac7d.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/f1335e5420fe6e475cded1092e9b1ba621e0d88f46110b69ffef5e35ed080d6e.png)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=2x\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/a53bb4e6cd7552b92424b168d0cda90fa1085b5e72fbf8a3c37a3a948bdcf9ad.png)\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/923e79b665f4529e579776188731896e6ce301743394e2102132f2cee7f6eaa9.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332833/field-1" "q-332833/field-2" "q-332833/field-3" "q-332833/field-4" "q-332833/field-5" "q-332833/field-6" "q-332833/field-7" "q-332833/field-8" "q-332833/field-9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ada3a84a-f979-5aee-9422-7acb8e430c11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333159/field-1/cea67b11aa5c9fde5d9510d1cf20c495d804285e7a0b8769c1a0c458072e296f" :answer/id #uuid "ec98af45-0f67-5922-a2ce-2226adbe944a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333159/field-1/0b4fc2c65192b2cc173c4e8ad58547377955072334ed0e3f1143e195e81e3110" :answer/id #uuid "a335f46e-ba05-5ce6-866f-3882d14f0e87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333159/field-1/3271feb643933511cd7b0e1eb04d9a734d471e9f34975f85c7afcf6213418e66" :answer/id #uuid "3737205d-6266-58e9-a0fe-c6fc8d301db3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333159/field-1/ac225e037427ea7fdc6f7e879ac709452f853ca3432bb046292aaaf20fbd5565" :answer/id #uuid "4de2ac93-dfcd-5f38-9307-6b53aa79738f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333159/field-1" :an