db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333637/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "5be1814d-5ca0-54e7-996c-be1bd0dc437a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-333637/field-4/47b5e16428f6cc903ef4e40f0ded305cf4b2c6071376c9e87a33cc1a98eb9f04" :answer-field/choices ["q-333637/field-4/47b5e16428f6cc903ef4e40f0ded305cf4b2c6071376c9e87a33cc1a98eb9f04" "q-333637/field-4/22e8a0aa62bc24395706ed418c76a5ef3df41c0d85ee55b4553fc245a500b4aa" "q-333637/field-4/cef53e2f4f249e823b4999c806f3152f01b5aecabcf33f4f9df9ee55880449dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333637" :question/id #uuid "9eee4cc9-af63-536a-aed0-c7dcc751b64f" :question/math-academy-id "q-333637" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$\n{{field-1}} is {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=-x$ is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/a09d50fa36b2748fb1c65ed16e20d950afbbabc18884ff8718cf1571c4e13b0e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333637/field-1" "q-333637/field-2" "q-333637/field-3" "q-333637/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35492718-d2d7-5c9d-9c02-1ef6ae0445d0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333640/field-1/1b60731b1779c600d1abbdb8187409ffe4c69778f0a32954816f2e025ce2725f" :answer/id #uuid "59f9777e-4b3c-50f8-a5e6-78ff3a79c58f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333640/field-1/4d092fda865cba74a0ab80adb9b5a04b7f2fd55f4b558f785d6f342b479ec0f8" :answer/id #uuid "f2a6b7e3-ff52-56d9-8c93-ce1126b6d864" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333640/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "404e91c1-8a4b-529d-a64a-d5a197f1d3fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-333640/field-1/4d092fda865cba74a0ab80adb9b5a04b7f2fd55f4b558f785d6f342b479ec0f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-333640/field-1/1b60731b1779c600d1abbdb8187409ffe4c69778f0a32954816f2e025ce2725f" "q-333640/field-1/4d092fda865cba74a0ab80adb9b5a04b7f2fd55f4b558f785d6f342b479ec0f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333640/field-2/861981e024e897416682817ca9e79c6d1e8ed9b541c7efe134d14879c4bffd